---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Ornament from '../components/Ornament.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="AlbionForge privacy policy: no cookies, no tracking, no accounts, no market data uploaded. Every calculation runs locally in your browser."
  canonical="/privacy/"
>
  <div class="crumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> › Privacy</div>
  <section class="section prose">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="lead">Short version: we can't track you, because nothing about you ever leaves your browser.</p>

    <h2>No cookies, no analytics, no accounts</h2>
    <p>
      AlbionForge is a fully static website. The calculators are plain scripts that run inside your
      browser. The prices you type are never sent anywhere - there is no server, no database and no
      account system behind them. We set no cookies and load no third-party analytics, ads or
      tracking scripts.
    </p>

    <h2>What is collected</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Nothing you enter.</strong> Prices, quantities and settings live only in the page
        (and in your browser's local storage if you use the “remember inputs” toggle, which stays
        on your device).
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Standard hosting logs.</strong> Our host (Cloudflare Pages) processes requests to
        serve the site and may keep short-lived technical logs, as any web host does. We do not use
        them to profile visitors.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Local storage</h2>
    <p>
      Calculators may remember your last inputs using your browser's local storage purely for
      convenience. This data never leaves your device and you can clear it at any time via your
      browser settings.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy ever changes materially (for example if an optional analytics service were
      added), the change will be noted here with a date.
    </p>

    <Ornament />
    <p class="small">
      Questions? See the <a href="/about/">About page</a> for what AlbionForge is (and is not).
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
